"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with a focus on leveraging AI for data visualization and secure file sharing. Key milestones include the approval of a $2M budget (later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses), the completion of the design phase, and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, and specialized training for coding teams and project managers has been approved with a $15,000 budget. Current phases involve development led by Omar Jensen and upcoming user interface enhancements planned for October."
